for seven years gerald mccarthy's dog  molly helped him cope with the sudden  death of his wife  but in february molly was snatched from  his garden in broad daylight  and gerald says that losing her  companionship was a huge blow  she was part my life big part of my life  massive part of my life  you know the first thing when i finished  work every day was just  you know you wanted to get on for molly  and um my day old  all my all my days were just revolved  around you know looking after molly and  that's what they are they're part of  your life  bit like family yeah absolutely  absolutely well she was my little girl  but legally  pets are classed as property so when  they're taken it's no different to a  stolen bike  and for katie stickley whose dog trigger  was returned by the police  eight months after he was stolen this  doesn't reflect the emotional bond  between  pets and their owners it should be  classed as kidnapped because it's a  living person  even though it's not a human it's still  living  and it's still part of the family i felt  sick like that someone's actually done  that  um felt  like shaky and helpless that you can't  do nothing like it was like if one of  your children was to get stolen  on monday parliament will debate  proposals that could make it  easier for stolen pets to be reunited  with their rightful owners  like making microchip scanning  compulsory for vets  but many want the government to go  further and a petition to make  dog theft a specific offence with a  minimum two year sentence  has got more than half a million  signatures the current legislation isn't  tough enough  people can steal a pet and they might  get a fine maybe a 120 pounds something  like that  rather than you know face the full force  of the law  and that's because it doesn't take into  consideration you know the traumatic  effect it has on the family so  what we wanted to do is have the law  recognize the trauma  that's caused in a family by having a  pet stolen and  an appropriate sentence in that  situation  gerald now has a new dog but says that  nothing can replace molly he  and many others want robust punishment  for those who steal beloved pets  milanovinovic sky news
 

